Package: rbeam
Type: Package
Title: Benchmark Evaluation and Metrics (R Interface)
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Izaskun", "Mallona", email = "izaskun.mallona.work@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-2853-7526"))
    )
Description: Thin R interface to the beam Python package. beam is a metric
    formalization layer for bioinformatics benchmarks: it ships metric cards
    (YAML, JSON Schema) with measurement-theory grounded metadata (scale type,
    polarity, range, allowed transformations), a multi-criteria decision
    analysis pipeline with sensitivity primitives (SMAA, leave-one-out,
    Triantaphyllou-Sanchez weight perturbation, the Skillings-Mack
    coverage-aware Friedman test), and method-dataset heterogeneity
    diagnostics (mixed-effects variance decomposition, Bradley-Terry trees,
    Plackett-Luce models). This R package exposes the canonical Python
    implementation via 'reticulate'.
URL: https://github.com/imallona/beam
